WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.645
Priya adds disability coverage for her twenty employees.

00:00:03.645 --> 00:00:08.657
A group plan differs from Rosa’s individual policy in predictable ways.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:13.669
The employer holds the master contract and often pays the premium.

00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:19.137
There is no individual medical underwriting; everyone in the class is covered.

00:00:19.137 --> 00:00:22.782
Benefits are a percentage of salary rather than

00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:26.427
a chosen dollar amount, with a monthly maximum.

00:00:26.427 --> 00:00:31.439
Coverage is usually nonoccupational and offsets Social Security and workers compensation.

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:37.363
Definitions tend to be split: own occupation for two years, then any occupation.

00:00:37.363 --> 00:00:41.464
If the employer pays the premium, benefits are taxable.

00:00:41.464 --> 00:00:46.020
Coverage ends when employment ends, though some plans allow conversion.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.749
Short-term disability replaces income during the first weeks of a disability.

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:54.618
Typical plans pay 60 to 70 percent of weekly

00:00:54.618 --> 00:00:58.057
salary for 13 to 26 weeks, sometimes 52.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:02.356
The elimination period is short, often zero days for accidents

00:01:02.356 --> 00:01:06.655
and seven for sickness, so benefits begin almost at once.

00:01:06.655 --> 00:01:10.524
Many employers self-fund STD because claims are frequent, small

00:01:10.524 --> 00:01:14.393
and predictable, hiring an insurer only to administer them.

00:01:14.393 --> 00:01:19.982
STD usually dovetails with sick leave, beginning when paid sick days run out.

00:01:19.982 --> 00:01:24.711
For Priya’s bakery, STD keeps a worker recovering from surgery on

00:01:24.711 --> 00:01:29.010
the payroll for the three months it takes to heal.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.691
Long-term disability begins where STD ends.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:37.052
The elimination period is 90 or 180 days, matched to the STD

00:01:37.052 --> 00:01:41.967
benefit period so the two plans hand off without a gap.

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:47.329
Benefits replace 50 to 67 percent of salary up to a monthly

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:52.690
cap, reduced by Social Security, workers compensation and other income, and continue

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:57.158
to age 65 or the Social Security normal retirement age.

00:01:57.158 --> 00:02:00.733
The definition is usually split at 24 months.

00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:06.094
Pre-existing condition limits are common, for example excluding conditions treated in the

00:02:06.094 --> 00:02:11.456
three months before coverage if disability begins within the first twelve months.

00:02:11.456 --> 00:02:15.030
LTD is almost always insured rather than self-funded.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:19.166
Priya’s head baker developed the recipes that built the business.

00:02:19.166 --> 00:02:24.956
If he is disabled, revenue falls and a replacement must be recruited and trained.

00:02:24.956 --> 00:02:29.091
Key employee disability income insurance pays the business a monthly

00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:33.227
benefit or lump sum while the key person is disabled.

00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:36.536
The business is the applicant, owner, premium payer

00:02:36.536 --> 00:02:39.844
and beneficiary; the key employee is the insured.

00:02:39.844 --> 00:02:44.807
The benefit funds a temporary replacement, covers lost profits and buys time.

00:02:44.807 --> 00:02:48.529
Premiums are not deductible, and benefits are received tax-free.

00:02:48.529 --> 00:02:52.251
The key person’s own disability income is a separate

00:02:52.251 --> 00:02:55.560
matter, handled by his personal or group coverage.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:01.444
If Rosa, a sole proprietor, is disabled, her income stops but the

00:03:01.444 --> 00:03:06.837
shop rent, utilities, employee wages, insurance premiums and loan payments continue.

00:03:06.837 --> 00:03:13.211
A business overhead expense policy reimburses those actual fixed expenses while the owner

00:03:13.211 --> 00:03:19.584
is disabled, up to a monthly maximum, for a short benefit period of

00:03:19.584 --> 00:03:25.468
one or two years, after a short elimination period, often 30 days.

00:03:25.468 --> 00:03:29.881
It does not pay the owner’s own salary or

00:03:29.881 --> 00:03:33.803
lost profit; her personal disability policy does that.

00:03:33.803 --> 00:03:39.686
BOE premiums are tax-deductible as a business expense, and benefits are taxable,

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:45.570
but the expenses they pay are deductible, which nets to little tax.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.856
Priya and her partner agree in writing that if either

00:03:48.856 --> 00:03:51.813
is permanently disabled, the other will buy her share.

00:03:51.813 --> 00:03:54.113
A disability buyout policy funds that purchase.

00:03:54.113 --> 00:03:58.713
After a long elimination period, typically one or two years so that the disability

00:03:58.713 --> 00:04:03.314
is clearly permanent, the policy pays a lump sum or installments to the business

00:04:03.314 --> 00:04:07.585
or the healthy partner, who uses it to buy out the disabled owner.

00:04:07.585 --> 00:04:10.214
Premiums are not deductible and benefits are tax-free.

00:04:10.214 --> 00:04:14.157
The arrangement gives the disabled owner cash for her interest and gives

00:04:14.157 --> 00:04:18.100
the business a clean transfer, mirroring the life insurance funded buy-sell agreement.
